  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smart Cities Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The consortium Smart City Kenya will test the Upande Non-Revenue Water (NRW) system. This innovative combination of hardware and software aims to reduce water losses of utility systems through real-time, automatic water flow/pressure measurement. At the same time, consumers will be able to view their water consumption data via their smartphones. The consortium consists of Upande BV, TagMeter Systems BV, Kisumu Water and Sanitation Company Lt., KIWASCO and Runda Water.</narrative>
  </description>
